Maintain minimum tails and binary-search for the first tail greater than or equal to each value. Replacing equal values ensures the subsequence is strictly increasing; empty input returns 0.

```javascript
function solve(nums) {
  const tails = [];

  for (const value of nums) {
    let left = 0;
    let right = tails.length;

    while (left < right) {
      const mid = left + Math.floor((right - left) / 2);
      if (tails[mid] < value) {
        left = mid + 1;
      } else {
        right = mid;
      }
    }

    tails[left] = value;
  }

  return tails.length;
}
```

Call solve(nums) directly with an integer array. Time: O(n log n); auxiliary space: O(n).

